[PACKAGE]:      GIT

[ALIAS]:        -git | -g

[AVAILABLE COMMANDS]:          

    -git dir :              Returns the Bitbucket Git address of the current directory stored in the .env file.
                            Return error if the current directory does not have an .env file.

    -git global :           Add the email and user to the GIT config file.

    -git init :             Initial commit to the GIT repository on Bitbucket.

    -git update :           Update the GIT repository in Bitbucket, requires a message at the end of the 
                            command to identify the commit.

    -git cache.password :   Adds the identity of the Bitbucket user to the cache.

    -git remove.dir :       Delete the .git directory in the current directory.

    -git rm :               Removes a remote from a local repository.

    -git safe.directory:    Add the repository directory as a safe directory with the recommended command.


